Z||000004||Black88GT||09-06-2000||11:21 PM||||The only thing I don't like about Saturns is they are OHC, read NO TORQUE.  They are definitely the most reliable American car ever made, however.  I think there is no excuse for people who don't buy American cars after the Saturns debut.  Actually, I am trying to talk my mother into getting one since her Buick just blew a tranny!<P><BR><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD||||reg||14
Z||000005||Oreif||09-07-2000||02:58 AM||||May not have a lot of torque but gas mileage is great and Saturn always puts the customer first! I bought this car used 4 years ago and Saturn still offered me all the perks that the new car buyers get! Like free carwashes. It is nice during the winter when the car gets dirty you just stop in and they run it thru the carwash and vacuum it! No cost! I had the alternator go out on it about 2 years ago. They came to my house and picked the car up, repaired it and brought it back to me. I cannot say enough about the service I recieved from them. If it wasn't for the kids growing up so fast I'd keep it. I just needed a bigger vehicle for the kids and I can't afford the new LS series cars right now.||||reg||1
Z||000006||ChadMan||09-07-2000||09:13 AM||||My wife has a 1995 SL1 - 107K miles, looks and runs great.  She went to the FOCOA Nationals in Nashville with me in 1997 and after we toured the Saturn plant, she said she wanted one!  We've had it 2 years and it's been very reliable (knock on plastic).||||reg||14
Z||000007||Black88GT||09-07-2000||10:41 PM||||Oreif, I heard the LS series wasn't selling to well so you might be able to get a good deal.  My friend bought a saturn and they have "customer appreciation nights".  That impressed me.  He went last time and they had tons of free food and he won 3 free oil changes.  There customer service is definitely top notch.<P><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD||||reg||14
